# GitHub Release Workflow

When the user asks to push a release, do all of the following:

- Bump the package version as requested and commit the release changes.
- Create and push the matching git tag, for example `v2.0.3`.
- Create or update the GitHub Release object with `gh release create ... --latest` or `gh release edit ... --latest`.
- Verify with `gh release list --limit 3` that the new version is marked `Latest`.

Pushing a git tag alone is not enough; GitHub's visible release version changes only after the GitHub Release exists.
